<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Inspire RH56DFTP right hand — fragment included by combined and standalone files.
     Root link: right_hand_base_link
     Every link has one visual per colour (black, white, silver), each on its own
     mesh in meshes/hand_right/visual/, and the whole link mesh as collision; see
     "Hand colours" in the README.
     Actuated joints (6): right_thumb_swing_joint, right_thumb_1_joint,
       right_index_1_joint, right_middle_1_joint, right_ring_1_joint, right_little_1_joint
     Coupled joints (6): right_thumb_2_joint, right_thumb_3_joint, right_index_2_joint,
       right_middle_2_joint, right_ring_2_joint, right_little_2_joint. How they follow the
       actuated joints depends on the xacro argument `coupling`:
         coupling:=mimic (default)  <mimic> tags: thumb_2 = 0.601 x thumb_1,
             thumb_3 = 0.579 x thumb_1, finger *_2 = 0.890 x *_1. Linear, so an
             approximation of the real hand (fingertips within 3 mm of it).
         coupling:=software  no <mimic>: the 12 joints are independent and the code
             that publishes them computes each one from the command with the curves
             measured on the real hand (config/hand_coupling.yaml, read by
             scripts/hand_coupling.py and scripts/hand_coupling_node.py). Every
             joint's limits are its curve's range, from the same file.
       See "Software coupling" in the README.

     The 12 digit links and joints are the EXACT MIRROR of inspire_hand_left
     across the y=0 plane of the palm: frame_right = S · frame_left · S with
     S = diag(1,-1,1), so origin xyz (x,y,z) -> (x,-y,z), origin rpy (r,p,y) ->
     (-r,p,-y), axis (x,y,z) -> (-x,y,-z) and inertia ixy,iyz negated. The
     meshes in meshes/hand_right/ (except base_link.STL) are the left meshes
     with y negated. Edit the LEFT hand and re-mirror; do not edit these by
     hand. right_hand_base_link (the palm) is the vendor's own export.
     Palm mass is set from a scale reading of the real hand: 0.840 kg for the
     whole hand, wrist flange included. The 12 digits keep their exported
     0.143381 kg, so the palm carries 0.840 - 0.143381 = 0.696619 kg. The
     deficit went to the palm because that is where the six actuators, the
     gearboxes, the controller and the wiring sit, and because the CAD export
     left almost every link at SolidWorks' default 1000 kg/m3. The flange in
     the palm mesh is the 16 mm one of the RH56DFTP-2 (the vendor's 30 mm
     flange, shortened; see the README). The centre of mass is unchanged and
     the tensor is scaled by 0.696619/0.314091 = 2.217891, which keeps the
     vendor's mass distribution. Both palms carry the same values, mirrored.

     q=0 is the hand FULLY OPEN (ANGLE_SET = 1000) and the upper limit is FULLY
     CLOSED (ANGLE_SET = 0) on all 12 joints, so every joint closes as q grows.

     ZEROS and UPPER LIMITS come from photos of the real hand at nine ANGLE_SET
     values per DOF (1000, 875, ... 0; inspire_hand_interface/Caracterizacion/
     imagenes/angulos limite/*_positions). This model was rendered in MuJoCo
     through a virtual camera fitted to each photo, and the joint values were
     swept until the rendered silhouette matched the photographed one
     (config/hand_coupling_measurements.yaml). Every joint origin is rotated so
     that q=0 is where the photos put that joint at ANGLE_SET = 1000.

     The RH56DFTP user manual, section 2.6.11 (printed pages 21 and 22), gives
     one chord angle per DOF against the metacarpal plane: alpha (fingers),
     theta (thumb bending) and beta (thumb rotation). Open, it says 176, 70 and
     165 deg; this model gives 172.3, 71.4 and 162.7 at q=0. Closed, the real
     hand stops short of the manual's angles (table below).

     Earlier versions put q=0 on the manual's open angles. The photographed
     open hand then sat at finger *_1 0.0571, *_2 0.0108, thumb_1 0.1257,
     thumb_2 -0.2074, thumb_3 -0.0868 and thumb_swing 0.0400 rad, and the
     origins were rotated by exactly those angles about each joint's axis. No
     pose changed, only the numbers that name it: q_now = q_before - offset.

     The table and everything below in this comment describe coupling:=mimic.
     With q=0 on the photographed open hand, its q_max and multipliers put
     each digit exactly where the photos put it both fully open and fully
     closed:

     | DOF            | q_max (rad) | multiplier      | closed angle   | manual closed |
     | fingers        | 1.517       | *_2: 0.890      | alpha 34 to 40 | alpha 20      |
     | thumb bending  | 0.624       | thumb_2: 0.601  | theta 19.8     | theta -13     |
     |                |             | thumb_3: 0.579  |                |               |
     | thumb rotation | 1.200       |                 | beta 94.0      | beta 90       |

     The real coupling is not linear (finger q2/q1 about 0.67 at mid travel and
     0.89 closed) and a mimic is. So the table below does not give the real
     proximal angle: it gives the actuated value that best places the fingertip
     at each command (at ANGLE_SET = 500 the real finger sits at 0.975 / 0.658,
     the table gives 0.889 with 0.791 distal). At its points the fingertips
     land within 2.0 mm (fingers) and 0.2 mm (thumb) of the real ones, exactly
     on them fully open and fully closed; between points, within 3.1 mm. The
     vendor's finger multiplier 1.05 folded the distal phalanx into the palm;
     the earlier values, with q=0 on the manual's angles (1.574 / 0.865 and
     0.75 / 0.224 / 0.367, and before them 1.62 / 0.85 and 0.66 / 0.40 / 0.60),
     left the fingertips up to 7 and 14 mm off.

     The SDK scale is NOT linear in the joints. With coupling:=software the
     mapping ANGLE_SET -> joints is config/hand_coupling.yaml. For
     coupling:=mimic, interpolate the actuated joints linearly between these
     points, with s = 1 - ANGLE_SET/1000 (thumb rotation within 3.5 deg):

     | s            | 0 | 0.25  | 0.5   | 0.75  | 1     |
     | finger *_1   | 0 | 0.519 | 0.889 | 1.194 | 1.517 |
     | thumb_1      | 0 | 0.159 | 0.334 | 0.497 | 0.624 |
     | thumb_swing  | 0 | 0.320 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 1.200 |  -->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!-- coupling:=mimic (default) | software. Unknown values stop xacro with a KeyError. -->
  <xacro:arg name="coupling" default="mimic"/>
  <xacro:property name="hand_coupling_software" value="${dict(mimic=False, software=True)['$(arg coupling)']}"/>
  <xacro:property name="hand_coupling_limits"
                  value="${xacro.load_yaml('$(find h1_2_inspire_description)/config/hand_coupling.yaml')['limits']}"/>

  <link name="right_hand_base_link">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.00826856171690858 -0.115495645683634 -0.0283405186091888" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.696619298523196"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.000599173537715081" ixy="-3.03890781389993E-06" ixz="1.43138854357359E-06"
               iyy="0.000714743287404168" iyz="3.77582394519895E-05" izz="0.000355919460629158"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://h1_2_inspire_description/meshes/hand_right/visual/right_hand_base_black.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="inspire_black">
        <color rgba="0.1 0.1 0.1 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://h1_2_inspire_description/meshes/hand_right/visual/right_hand_base_white.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="inspire_white">
        <color rgba="0.93 0.93 0.93 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://h1_2_inspire_description/meshes/hand_right/visual/right_hand_base_silver.STL"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="inspire_silver">
        <color rgba="0.60 0.61 0.64 1"/>
      </material>
    </visual>
    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://h1_2_inspire_description/meshes/hand_right/base_link.STL"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <link name="right_thumb_swing">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="-0.001897403655087 7.12516796909923E-05 0.00313589310434412" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.00115518743162309"/>
      <inertia ixx="6.27834293959477E-08" ixy="-9.38445541803444E-10" ixz="-3.50236810587605E-09"
               iyy="3.78279141131513E-08" iyz="1.31528360070952E-10" izz="6.1816168438865E-08"/>
